  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ed 1123.18 Hearing Officer Decision",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1123.18 Hearing Officer Decision.\n\n(a) Requests for findings of fact shall be limited to those facts necessary to support the decision.\n\n(b) Requests for rulings of law shall be limited to those central issues of law, if any, which are contested or essential.\n\n(c) The hearing officer shall render a decision, including findings of facts and rulings of law consistent with RSA 541-A:35.\n\n(d) Any party aggrieved by the decision of the hearing officer may appeal the decision as provided in Ed 1123.20.\n\n(e) The department shall ensure that not later than 45 days after the time for conducting an administrative due process hearing in Ed 1123.09:\n\n(1) A final decision is reached in the hearing consistent with RSA 541-A:35; and\n\n(2) A copy of the decision is sent by certified mail to each of the parties.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
}
